 # @openfilm/desktop
+
+## 0.2.0
+
+### Minor Changes
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Saved: your own library, the same in every project. The bookmark button beside Upload switches the media pane to it, and back; it is the same pane, so upload, folders, list and grid, filters, sort, search, rename, move and delete all work there, and anything can go in it: video, pictures, sound, documents, any file. Right-click a clip on the timeline or the picture, or a file of the project, and choose Add to Saved; with several clips selected, save them as one (they come back on tracks of their own, laid out as they were, links kept) or each alone. Drag anything from Saved onto the timeline, or press Enter: a file is imported into the project as one from your computer is, and a saved clip comes back as you saved it, with its place, its look and the changes made in its page, its files copied into the project, so changing it there never changes the saved one. Saved is a folder beside your projects (Movies/OpenFilm/Saved on a Mac), so you can also add to it from Finder. The media pane no longer has a close button: the assets button beside the chat opens and closes it.
+
+  Template: select a page clip and the inspector shows what its page lets you change, without opening the page: each of its words, each of its pictures (replace one with a picture of the project, one dropped from the media pane, or one from your computer), and the CSS custom properties its stylesheet sets on `:root` (a color with a color picker, a number with its unit, a font with the font picker, words in quotes as text). Each change is kept for that clip only, and one changed can go back to the page's own. A page saved with such properties is marked as a template in Saved.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Tabs: the desktop window keeps each open project in a tab of its own, in Studio's top bar, side by side, the one in front in the panes' color. `+` (⌘T) opens the projects window, and the project picked opens in a new tab (or comes forward, when it is open already). ⌘W closes a tab, ⇧⌘T opens the last one closed again, ⌘1–9 and ⌃Tab switch. A tab shows when an agent is working in it, when one is waiting for your answer, and an export's progress; agents and exports go on in tabs behind. The tabs come back as you left them; with none open, the window shows your projects. The projects window has two views: your projects, and Examples, where example films play their preview under the pointer and open on a page of their own with their parts, to start a new film from. Skills show their own title and summary in your language (a skill's optional `openfilm.json`). An examples index can list each example's `category`, `segments` and a `video` preview; one read from a file has its pictures served by Studio. Studio in a browser keeps its projects window, now with the same two views.
+
+### Patch Changes
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - In OpenFilm an agent keeps its maker's own MCP servers, but the ones you added to it yourself stay off until you turn each on. The switches are in Settings → Agents, under the agent; this covers Claude Code (its claude.ai connectors stay), Codex, OpenCode, Qwen Code, Gemini CLI and Copilot. Your own skills now stay off in Qwen Code and Gemini CLI too, and Copilot and Qwen Code get OpenFilm's skills. Claude Code's skill filter no longer waits for a first session to learn its skills.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - `openfilm get asr` now keeps the transcript beside any recording in the project, not only those under `assets/`. A file at the top of the project, or a reference video in `references/`, gets its WebVTT too. Before, none was kept and the answer wrongly said the service does not time words. In Studio, making subtitles now works for a clip whose file is outside `assets/`: before, it was transcribed on every try and nothing was kept. Files and folders starting with a dot (`.git`) belong to the tools, so a recording there is refused before anything is sent.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio: a click on the picture takes what is under a full-frame overlay. When the clip on top has nothing there but a layer filling its page (a letterbox, a vignette, grain laid over the film), the click, the hover outline and a double-click to type go to the title or picture under it in the clip below. Before, the overlay's clip was taken and nothing under it could be picked in the picture.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: when Codex is installed more than once, as a command installed long ago and the copy inside the Codex or ChatGPT app (or a Microsoft Store app), the newer one is used: the models Codex offers depend on its version, so an old copy showed only a few. On Windows, a reason Codex could not start is readable instead of `������` on a system in Chinese or another non-English language.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: when Codex is found but can't start, the chat's model menu now says why, in Codex's own words, instead of only "Couldn't start it to read its settings". A Codex older than the chat needs says to update it. Settings → Agents no longer shows Codex as connected when it can't read its own config file, and names the setting it could not read.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: a file added to the message you are writing opens to look at, as one in a sent message does: click a video to play it, a picture to see it large, a text to read it.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: the files added to the message you are writing show in whole rows, up to three at once, so a message's twelve files are all in view. Before, the second row was cut in half and had to be scrolled to.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio's preview no longer flashes at a cut. A page coming on used to show before its frame was drawn, so for a moment it showed how it looked before: its first state, or the frame it drew the last time it was on. Now it shows once that frame is drawn, and the picture before it stays until then. Exports were never affected.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - The Examples and the skills show at once. OpenFilm comes with a copy of the examples index and its posters, and keeps the last index it read, so the Examples tab no longer waits on GitHub (a slow or blocked connection showed nothing); the newest index is read in the background as Studio starts. A gallery opened again shows what it read before while it asks again, skill covers and example posters stay in the browser's cache, and the app reads what the composer's skills need as it starts.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio: words typed into a line in the picture show in the inspector as they are typed. Its text box and the layer's name follow each key, and go back to the old words when the edit is given up with Esc. Before, the inspector kept the old words until Enter.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: Your own key works again. The 0.1.7 installer carried newer versions of the agent's packages than the ones tested, one of which no longer fit, so every message ended with "ACP connection closed". The installer now carries exactly the versions in the lockfile, and its build stops if any differ.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Settings → Agents: an agent that is connected shows Disconnect alone. Locate… is offered when it is disconnected (beside Connect) or not found.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio: a theme change reaches everything at once. The audio meters beside the timeline and the clips' waveforms are drawn again in the new theme's colors (before, they kept the other theme's, such as dark meter bars in the light theme, until the film played), and every other open page of Studio, such as another tab of the app, takes the theme too.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Your own key's agent gets a shorter system prompt with no conflicting instructions. It was told both that it already had the manual and that it should print it, and both to open Studio and never to open it. Rules it got two or three times are now said once. Its own part is a third shorter, and the manual is unchanged.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: Your own key is an agent with models of your own, each set up on its own: the name the chat shows, the API format and address of its service, its own key, the model asked for there, and the reasoning efforts it takes. The chat's model menu switches between them, from one service to another, as it does for the other agents. A model on an address already set up can take that model's key. Models set up before become one each, on the service and key they had.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Settings: Models is now Services (which service makes each kind of media), and your own services moved there as Custom services. One is set up with its name, address, key and a description of what it does and how it is called (or where its API docs are): where the key goes is no longer asked, since your agent puts it where the service's docs say.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Settings say what is there now: Custom services take as many services as you like, and say you can also tell your agent about a service in the chat (one with a key is better set up there, so the key stays out of the conversation). The note pointing to the old "Your own services" is gone, Agents describes your own key as models you set up, Providers says the choice of each kind of media is under Services, and the sign-in wait no longer names Terminal (Windows opens PowerShell).
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Skills: ways of making a kind of film, each a folder with a SKILL.md and the files it brings. `openfilm skills` lists the skills a film can be made with: the project's own (in its `skills/` folder), yours (in `~/Movies/OpenFilm/Skills`), and the official ones. `openfilm skill <name>` prints one for the agent to follow. `openfilm skill add <GitHub address or folder>` adds a skill to yours and lists any scripts it brings. The manual tells agents about them. Studio no longer lists pages inside a project's `skills/` folder.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - In the chat, a skill can be named in a message: type `/`, or pick one in the Community; it goes in as a pill and the agent gets the skill's instructions with the message. The composer's Community button opens over your film on the skills (official, yours, this project's), with the examples beside them: point the agent at an example, or a part of one (a segment, or a stretch dragged on its strip), and it reads how that film is made; or start a new film from it, in a tab of its own. Add a skill there from a GitHub link or a folder, or make one with the agent. In OpenFilm an agent keeps its maker's own skills and gets OpenFilm's, but the skills you installed in it yourself stay off until you turn each on in Settings → Agents. This works for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and your own key's agent; agents that can't be told say they use all of yours. The context ring is gone: when a conversation is nearly full, a line above the composer offers a new one.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop on Windows: skills work. The app loaded its skills module by a Windows path, which Node refuses, so the Skills button and gallery could not read skills and agents started without OpenFilm's.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Your own skills are kept in `~/Movies/OpenFilm/Skills` (beside Projects and Exports, backed up with them); skills kept in `~/.openfilm/skills` move there on their own. A skill replaced or removed goes to the trash, never deleted, and `openfilm skill remove <name>` moves one there. Adding from a link or a folder shows what came first: each skill, its size, the scripts it brings and any of yours it would replace, then Add or Cancel. The switches for an agent's own skills are in Settings → Agents, beside its MCP servers. OpenFilm's own skill for terminal agents is no longer shown in the app.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio: a project with thousands of files plays smoothly as soon as it opens. While its files' lengths and sizes were read, each answer laid out the media pane again (tens of ms with that many files), so the picture stalled again and again for the first minutes. The answers now come in a few times a second, and the pane works out its folders in one pass.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Desktop: stopping the agent while a command it ran was still going no longer starts a turn of its own a moment later, "A background task finished; the agent went on", that Stop could not end. The rest of a command from a turn that already ended (its last output, its exit) now stays out of the chat. Stop ends a turn the agent started by itself at once. Such a turn that ends with nothing in it leaves no line behind, including ones already saved.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Choose where new projects go. Settings → General → Storage shows the folder, with the free space on its disk, and lets you change it (or go back to the default), for example to keep large projects off a full system disk. Exports go where you pick when exporting, as before. New projects, including ones fetched with `openfilm open`, go to the folder you choose; projects made before stay where they are and still open from the list. On Windows, the installer now asks where to install the app.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio: a short clip's thumbnails fill it. Each picture in a clip's row was squeezed to the clip's width while the pictures kept their places, so the clip's color showed between them and the row looked broken.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - A turn's log (Settings → Developer) now shows everything the agent and its model got. A new "Sent to the agent" tab shows how the app started the agent, every word it adds to the agent's own instructions, and each message exactly as the agent got it, with its pictures. Model requests are no longer only your own key's: for Claude Code, Codex and Kimi they are read from each agent's own record. Each request shows its full system prompt, its tools, every message (including what the agent added by itself: project instructions, environment, skill lists, reminders), the answer and its tokens. Subagents' requests are included. Turns from before this change show their requests too, as long as the agent's record is still there.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - A turn's log (Settings → Developer) now shows model requests for Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, Qwen Code, CodeBuddy and OpenCode too: each request's system prompt, tools, every message (including what the agent added by itself), the answer and its tokens. With Developer mode on, Gemini CLI, Qwen Code, CodeBuddy and OpenCode are started with their own local logging switch, written into a folder of the app's and kept for a week. The app leaves any telemetry you set yourself as it is. CodeBuddy is logged only when its own telemetry is off (`DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`), since otherwise its traces would name each logged file. Copilot's requests are rebuilt from its own record, which has no tool definitions. Where a log lacks something, the viewer says so, and it explains a turn that has no requests (Cursor makes its prompt on its servers).
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - A turn's log shows how the session's skills and MCP servers were set: OpenFilm's skills, your own skills and servers kept off, and the ones you let in. A thought the agent did not keep in its record now says so, instead of showing 0 characters.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Studio run with npm updates itself: when a newer OpenFilm is out, Update appears in the top bar (and in Settings → About), and a click runs the newest in the background; Studio starts again on it and the page comes back on the new version. `openfilm update` does the same from a terminal, or for an agent asked to update OpenFilm. The desktop app's Studio still updates with the app.
+
+- [#58](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/58) [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - What's new: 0.1.7's notes, missing when it shipped, so Settings → About and Developer show them, and an update from 0.1.6 shows them once. Every version now has its notes before it can be released.
+
+- Updated dependencies [[`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`e70d9d9`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/e70d9d93c7bebe3d634ff2caa6f7a738cdde59d3), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`b138595`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/b138595d4c2d1fa5262b4a8a8c7cd98187c4b077), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`8ca326c`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/8ca326c24970fd6f639b3af064a0ea298ff2bdf6), [`b92c292`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/b92c29240b7fec2d9e993c23264eaf6ac593db5e)]:
